e-closeout.md\n?? reviews/P50-normal-faithful-corner-trace-recovery.md\n?? reviews/P50U-ultraweak-normality-bridge-closeout.md\n?? reviews/P51-full-finite-corner-central-exclusion-closeout.md\n?? reviews/P51-full-finite-corner-central-exclusion-recovery.md\n?? reviews/P53-local-hyperbolic-algebraic-alpha-closeout.md\n?? reviews/P55-regional-concrete-cstar-alpha-out-of-budget.md\n?? reviews/P55A-local-hyperbolic-finite-stage-uhf-bridge-closeout.md\n?? reviews/P58-mixed-uhf-hyperfinite-factor-closeout.md\n?? reviews/P60-full-corner-semifinite-weight-closeout.md\n?? reviews/P60R-full-corner-standard-semifiniteness-repair-closeout.md\n294:# Task Group: source-workspace two-lane Aristotle/Codex formalization autopilot\n296:scope: autonomous two-lane theorem formalization, terminal-status Codex closeout, safe artifact staging, and resource-bounded Lean verification\n303:- rollout_summaries/2026-08-06T14-29-28-EPRR-two_lane_aristotle_autopilot_closeout_hardening.md (cwd=source-workspace, rollout_path=<original-home>/.codex/sessions/2026/08/06/rollout-2026-08-06T16-29-28-019fd77a-ab18-78f3-a38a-968e45471677.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-06T18:07:30+00:00, thread_id=019fd77a-ab18-78f3-a38a-968e45471677, success: two-lane queues and compact manuscript staging verified)\n309:## Task 2: diagnose systemd and quarantine-closeout failures\n313:- rollout_summaries/2026-08-06T14-29-28-EPRR-two_lane_aristotle_autopilot_closeout_hardening.md (cwd=source-workspace, rollout_path=<original-home>/.codex/sessions/2026/08/06/rollout-2026-08-06T16-29-28-019fd77a-ab18-78f3-a38a-968e45471677.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-06T18:07:30+00:00, thread_id=019fd77a-ab18-78f3-a38a-968e45471677, partial: recovered closeout path; FF15/P37 advancement unverified)\n327:- The live runner is `work/aristotle_autopilot/aristotle_autopilot.py`, configured by `work/aristotle_autopilot/autopilot.toml`. It has independent finite-fiber FF15–FF23 and stabilizer-hyperfinite P37–P46 queues, one active Aristotle task per lane, Codex closeout only at terminal status, and advancement only after both machine-readable acceptance and decision fields. [Task 1]\n330:- Persist closeout metadata in `work/aristotle_autopilot/state.json` before starting Codex. An interrupted closeout without a machine-readable decision halts for review rather than retrying or advancing ambiguously. [Task 2]\n335:- symptom: a closeout consumes about 13 GB and clones/builds Mathlib -> cause: `lake build` was run in a stripped downloaded Aristotle quarantine snapshot with no `.lake` -> fix: inspect/quarantine there, copy only the reviewed candidate to the already-built live project, and run all Lean checks only in that live checkout. [Task 2]\n336:- status guard: at rollout end FF15 and P37 were still active. Do not claim candidate acceptance, FF15 integration, or FF16/P38 submission until `state.json`, closeout output/review, and live Lean checks agree. [Task 2]\n576:- when the user approved unattended automation and Telegram notifications -> halt and alert on blocked/failed/partial/unverified closeouts, but keep routine successful progress quiet [Task 3]\n1806:- For repo-root graph work, the quickest structural check is `python3 <original-home>/.codex/skills/project-graph-scheme/scripts/project_graph.py validate --graph project_graph.json`; closeout-quality verification then adds `python3 -m json.tool` on the JSON files, `jsonschema.validate(...)` or `jsonschema -i`, and locator audits when nodes point into real files [Task 2][Task 3][Task 4]\n1817:- symptom: graph closeouts overstate mathematical certainty -> cause: the graph is treated as a proof artifact instead of a provenance/navigation layer -> fix: state explicitly that the graph records the current support status and does not independently re-prove the mathematics [Task 2][Task 3]\n1898:- rollout_summaries/2026-07-15T13-22-01-YKcF-general_type_ii_stabilizer_criterion_workline.md (cwd=source-workspace, rollout_path=<original-home>/.codex/sessions/2026/07/15/rollout-2026-07-15T15-22-01-019f65f1-0246-7c83-9c24-dd45127a4929.jsonl, updated_at=2026-07-15T13:44:33+00:00, thread_id=019f65f1-0246-7c83-9c24-dd45127a4929, same rollout; distinct routing value for compile/verification and conditional-closeout guidance)\n1937:- symptom: first-pass LaTeX warnings look like unresolved problems at closeout -> cause: references only settle after a second pass -> fix: rerun `pdflatex` and report final-state warnings separately from first-pass noise [Task 2]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,260p' <original-home>/.codex/skills/aristotle-cli/SKILL.md && sed -n '1,260p' AGENTS.md && printf '\\\\n--- PLAN P55 context ---\\\\n' && rg -n -C 6 'P55B|P55|Lane H|H' PLAN.md && printf '\\\\n--- decision relevant ---\\\\n' && sed -n '1,260p' work/TWO-LANE-FORMALIZATION-DECISION.md && printf '\\\\n--- packet ---\\\\n' && sed -n '1,320p' aristotle_tasks/P55B-local-hyperbolic-source-uhf-bridge.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,260p' <original-home>/.codex/skills/aristotle-cli/SKILL.md && sed -n '1,260p' AGENTS.md && printf '\\\\n--- PLAN P55 context ---\\\\n' && rg -n -C 6 'P55B|P55|Lane H|H' PLAN.md && printf '\\\\n--- decision relevant ---\\\\n' && sed -n '1,260p' work/TWO-LANE-FORMALIZATION-DECISION.md && printf '\\\\n--- packet ---\\\\n' && sed -n '1,320p' aristotle_tasks/P55B-local-hyperbolic-source-uhf-bridge.md\"","aggregated_output":"---\nname: aristotle-cli\ndescription: Use when Codex should interact with the Aristotle CLI to submit Lean projects or papers, request sorry filling or formalization runs, inspect job status, and download results for iterative project work.\n---\n\n# Aristotle CLI\n\nUse Aristotle for remote Lean/project runs when the local repo is ready but needs automated proof search, sorry filling, or formalization help.\n\n## Workflow\n\n1. Confirm the target project or paper from the current workspace.\n2. Check the local build or project state first. Prefer a narrow local `lake build` or equivalent before submitting anything remote.\n3. Use the bundled wrapper `scripts/aristotle-auth.sh` unless `ARISTOTLE_API_KEY` is already known to be exported in the current process.\n4. Submit the smallest useful task prompt. Keep it concrete and tied to the files at hand.\n5. Wait for the result when that is useful. Otherwise poll or list jobs.\n6. Download artifacts, inspect the diffs, and rerun local verification.\n\n## Commands\n\nUse the commands in [references/aristotle-cli.md](references/aristotle-cli.md).\n\n## Operating rules\n\n- Prefer `aristotle submit` for Lean project work, especially sorry filling or proof search.\n- Prefer `aristotle formalize` when the input is a paper or TeX source that should become a Lean artifact.\n- Use `aristotle list` to inspect recent jobs and `aristotle download` to retrieve results.\n- Keep prompts specific: name the file, theorem, section, or proof obligation instead of asking for broad improvement.\n- If a run fails, inspect the local artifact and re-submit only after the prompt or project state is corrected.\n- Do not print or log the API key.\n- If authentication fails but `~/.bashrc` contains the key, do not assume sourcing `.bashrc` works. Many `.bashrc` files return early for noninteractive shells. Use `scripts/aristotle-auth.sh`.\n\n## When to escalate back to the user\n\n- The CLI is missing, or authentication still fails after trying `scripts/aristotle-auth.sh`.\n- The target repo is not a Lean project or paper and needs clarification.\n- The requested action would overwrite user work outside the target project tree.\n# Manuscript-Only Context Policy\n\n## Source authority\n\nFor manuscript-facing statements, the sole mathematical source is\n`sources/manuscript/main.tex`.\nThe local summary and locator record is `SOURCE-CONTRACT.md`. Do not modify\nthe manuscript from this project.\n\nEvery claim described as coming from the manuscript must identify an exact\nline range in `main.tex`. Repository history, earlier chat context, and other\nartifacts are not substitute sources.\n\n## Context firewall\n\nDo not introduce, assume, or attribute to the manuscript any gLU,\nrefinement, layer-coherence, or finite-coordinate construction unless it is\npresent in the cited manuscript lines or is explicitly introduced as a new\nauxiliary assumption. A Lean file compiling does not make its unstated\nphysical or operator-algebraic hypotheses part of the manuscript.\n\nClassify each item as one of:\n\n1. **manuscript-derived**: exact source locator and no stronger conclusion;\n2. **auxiliary assumption**: explicitly labelled and used only conditionally;\n3. **Lean infrastructure**: reusable formal mathematics that makes no source\n   claim; or\n4. **legacy exploratory work**: retained for reference but unavailable as\n   support for a manuscript-derived assertion.\n\n`CONTEXT-LEDGER.md` records the current legacy items.\n\n## Current formalization boundary\n\nThe target discussed in the manuscript is the short-range regional-algebra\nstatement at `main.tex:1740-1752`; its proposed proof is at\n`main.tex:1891-2004`. Keep separate the asserted algebraic identification,\nthe product-state/GNS steps, the unformalized operator-algebraic completion and\nspatial tensor-product steps, and the trace conclusion. A tracial state is\nappropriate only for the finite pure-sector case. The infinite pure-sector\ntarget instead calls for a faithful normal semifinite trace/weight when the\nrequired hypotheses and von Neumann infrastructure are supplied.\n\n## Aristotle task packets\n\nEvery new task under `aristotle_tasks/` must begin with exactly one context\ndeclaration:\n\n- `Source basis: main.tex:<line range>` for a manuscript-facing task; or\n- `Infrastructure only:` for reusable Lean material that makes no manuscript\n  claim.\n\nIt must then list every auxiliary assumption, state its exact Lean target, and\nsay whether its conclusion is conditional. A task may not cite a legacy\nartifact as its source basis. Use `aristotle_tasks/TEMPLATE.md` for new\npackets.\n\n## Active two-lane plan execution\n\nThe active Codex/Aristotle execution plan is `PLAN.md`, with the approval\nrecord in `work/TWO-LANE-FORMALIZATION-DECISION.md`. Before starting any new\npackage in the P47--P61 program, read both files and the closeout/audit record\nfor every declared predecessor.\n\nEvery future packet must include a `Plan alignment` section containing:\n\n1. the exact package identifier and its lane: `G` (general finite-corner and\n   central type-III exclusion), `H` (explicit local-hyperbolic tensor-factor\n   model), `shared`, or `reconnection`;\n2. the predecessor packages that have already been integrated, or `none` for\n   a foundation package;\n3. the exact gate this package is permitted to discharge; and\n4. downstream claims it is forbidden to make.\n\nThe Aristotle prompt must explicitly instruct the worker to read the active\nplan and respect this section. A package may use only integrated, compiled\npredecessors; a finished remote job is not a dependency until it has passed\nthe local semantic audit. Do not infer a theorem from a later package, and do\nnot submit a dependent packet before its listed prerequisites are integrated.\n\nFor Lane G, the required conclusion is a nonzero finite **projection** in\nevery nonzero central summand; a finite-dimensional subalgebra is not enough.\nFor Lane H, do not call the local algebra a factor until the spatial tensor\nfactorization and factorhood of both factors are proved. Neither lane may\nclaim a global trace/weight unless it constructs or explicitly assumes one.\n\n## Verification and reporting\n\nReport Lean compilation separately from mathematical validation. For each\nmanuscript-facing milestone, state which source clauses are represented, which\nassumptions remain external, and which analytic/von Neumann-algebraic claims\nare not yet formalized in the pinned Mathlib version.\n\n--- PLAN P55 context ---\n21-This lane does **not** require a direct-integral formalization or a global\n22-trace/weight on `M_Gamma`. A global faithful normal semifinite weight is a\n23-separate optional strengthening. The condition to formalize is the existence\n24-of a nonzero finite **projection/corner** in each nonzero central summand, not\n25-merely a finite-dimensional subalgebra.\n26-\n27:### Lane H — explicit local-hyperbolic tensor-factor model\n28-\n29-**Source basis:** `main.tex:1671-1679`, `main.tex:1898-2004`.\n30-\n31-From a coherent local hyperbolic basis, construct the finite coordinate maps,\n32-their coherent algebraic direct-limit star equivalence, concrete C-star\n33-models, the state identity, and the product GNS tensor splitting. Then prove\n--\n39-trivial-center/factor conclusion for this special case. This conclusion does\n40-not follow merely from the word \"hyperbolic\"; it follows from the constructed\n41-spatial factorization.\n42-\n43-### Reconnection\n44-\n45:Lane H gives an explicit factor theorem and, in the infinite-pure case, the\n46-concrete faithful normal semifinite weight `Tr barTensor tau`. Lane G gives\n47-the general no-central-type-III theorem. A final comparison theorem may show\n48:that the Lane-H factor model satisfies the Lane-G finite-corner criterion, but\n49-the two results remain logically independent.\n50-\n51-## Aristotle package sequence\n52-\n53-### Shared/central core\n54-\n--\n65-| P51 | `FullFiniteCornerCentralExclusion.lean` | Prove `q` finite, prove fullness, and derive `0 != z ->` a nonzero finite projection in `z M_Gamma`; define/use the project-local type-III obstruction. |\n66-\n67-### Explicit local-hyperbolic lane\n68-\n69-| Packet | Lean target | Purpose and acceptance gate |\n70-|---|---|---|\n71:| P52 | `CoherentLocalHyperbolicCoordinates.lean` | Build finite coordinate blocks and an exhaustion from local hyperbolic data. Audit whether finite support suffices; otherwise isolate the exact local-finiteness/coherence assumption. |\n72:| P53 | `LocalHyperbolicAlgebraicAlpha.lean` | Construct the finite stage maps, phase calibration, and coherent algebraic `alpha`; instantiate the existing direct-limit theorems without supplied stage equivalences. |\n73:| P54 | `UHFReferenceRepresentation.lean` | Construct a faithful compatible Hilbert/operator representation of the dyadic algebra from finite stages; do not assume an infinite tensor-product Hilbert space. |\n74:| P55A | `LocalHyperbolicFiniteStageUHFBridge.lean` | Construct, rather than assume, the finite-stage star equivalence from each P53 coordinate Pauli algebra to the corresponding finite dyadic matrix algebra, with explicit generator/phase formulas and norm control. |\n75:| P55B | `LocalHyperbolicSourceUHFBridge.lean` | Prove coherence of the P55A maps and identify the P53 source direct limit with the coordinate dyadic limit; prove the finite terminal-stage and infinite cofinal-UHF branches separately. |\n76:| P55C | `LocalHyperbolicConcreteRepresentations.lean` | Transport the P54 faithful representation through P55B and P53 alpha, and construct the source and regional closed operator-range C-star algebras with faithful dense embeddings. |\n77:| P55D | `RegionalConcreteCStarAlpha.lean` | Extend the P53 algebraic alpha uniquely between the P55C concrete C-star closures and prove the inverse and dense-range identities. |\n78:| P56 | `RegionalProductStateIdentity.lean` | After P55D, prove the stabilizer/product-state equality on finite Pauli words and extend it by density and continuity. |\n79:| P57 | `ProductGNSTensorFactorization.lean` | Construct the pure/mixed product GNS Hilbert-space tensor splitting and the spatial represented-algebra identification. |\n80:| P58 | `MixedUHFHyperfiniteFactor.lean` | Construct/prove the finite mixed matrix and infinite mixed hyperfinite-II1 alternatives under project-local factor and normal-trace definitions. |\n81:| P59 | `LocalHyperbolicFactorTraceTheorem.lean` | Transport P57--P58 to the regional algebra, prove trivial center, and state the finite-pure trace versus infinite-pure faithful-normal-semifinite-weight dichotomy. |\n82-\n83-### Optional strengthening/reconnection\n84-\n85-| Packet | Lean target | Purpose |\n86-|---|---|---|\n87-| P60 | `FullCornerSemifiniteWeight.lean` | Retired partial attempt: it constructs a conditional extended-positive trace series and finite-compression certificate, but does not yet prove standard positive-cone semifiniteness. |\n88-| P60R | `FullCornerSemifiniteWeight.lean` | Recovery: define the weight on the positive cone and prove standard semifiniteness using positive square roots and the finite comparison projections. |\n89:| P61 | `HyperbolicImpliesCentralCriterion.lean` | Show the explicit Lane-H model supplies the finite-corner criterion used by Lane G. |\n90-\n91-## Initial parallel wave\n92-\n93-Submit only the four independent foundation packets first: P47, P48, P52,\n94-and P54. Integrate and semantically audit them before submitting dependent\n95-packets. Existing P42--P46 task drafts are preserved as historical drafts;\n--\n113-7. P50's WOT-continuity theorem is a mathematically stronger certificate but\n114-   is not itself the standard definition of normality. P50U must formalize the\n115-   actual ultraweak topology and checked comparison before the project reports\n116-   the corner state as ultraweak-normal in the formal interface. P51's\n117-   finiteness/fullness proof is logically independent because it uses only\n118-   traciality and faithfulness.\n119:8. The original P55 exhausted its remote budget without producing its\n120:   authorized Lean file. It is retired, not accepted. P55A--P55D replace it\n121-   and expose the previously missing bridge between P53's twisted-Pauli direct\n122:   limit and P54's dyadic UHF model. P56 may advance only after P55D is\n123-   integrated and audited.\n124-\n125----\n126-\n127-# Previous single-lane plan: retained background\n128-\n\n--- decision relevant ---\n# Two-lane formalization decision\n\nDate: 2026-08-07\n\nThe active Codex/Aristotle loop follows the two-lane plan in `PLAN.md`.\n\n**Lane G** formalizes the manuscript's general-lattice corner argument:\nthe strong-limit code projection `q`, the faithful normal finite tracial state\non `q M_Gamma q`, finiteness and fullness of `q`, and the conclusion that each\nnonzero central summand has a nonzero finite projection and hence is not type\nIII. This route does not use a direct integral and does not require a global\ntrace/weight on `M_Gamma`.\n\n**Lane H** formalizes the explicit short-range/local-hyperbolic model:\ncoherent coordinate maps, an algebraic and C-star `alpha`, the product-state\nidentity, product GNS tensor factorization, and the resulting factor and\ntrace/weight classification.\n\nThe lanes meet only after their own gates are met. In particular, the explicit\ntensor-factor result proves trivial center in the special local-hyperbolic\ncase, whereas the general corner result rules out type-III central summands\nwithout asserting trivial center.\n\nThe first approved parallel Aristotle wave is P47, P48, P52, and P54. No\ndependent packet should be submitted before its prerequisite results are\nintegrated and semantically audited.\n\nAmendment, 2026-08-07: the analytic passage from the compressed quasi-local\nC-star algebra to the von Neumann corner is mandatory project infrastructure.\nAfter P48, the loop must prove strong closedness of concrete von Neumann\nalgebras (P49A), the analytic double-commutant theorem (P49B), and Kaplansky\nunit-ball density with its compressed-corner corollary (P49C). P50 depends on\nboth the finite-stage/C-star trace P49 and the proved P49C result. These core\nanalytic theorems may require new local topology machinery, but may not be\nreplaced by axioms or supplied interfaces.\n\nAmendment, 2026-08-08: P50's checked WOT continuity is retained as a stronger\nconcrete certificate, but the field name alone is not accepted as a\nformalization of the standard ultraweak definition of normality. Package P50U\nmust define the ultraweak topology from absolutely summable series of matrix\ncoefficients, prove the topology comparison, and export an explicitly\nultraweak-normal P50 conclusion. This does not block P51's finite-projection\nargument, which uses the corner state's traciality and faithfulness rather than\nnormality.\n\nAmendment, 2026-08-08: the original P55 is retired after Aristotle returned\n`OUT_OF_BUDGET` without creating `RegionalConcreteCStarAlpha.lean`. The failed\nrun is not evidence and no code from it is integrated. Lane H now uses four\nseparate gates: P55A constructs finite-stage Pauli-to-dyadic equivalences,\nP55B proves coherence and the finite/infinite direct-limit identifications,\nP55C constructs faithful source/regional operator representations and their\nclosed ranges, and P55D extends the algebraic alpha by density. This split is\nmathematical: P53 and P54 did not yet contain an identification between their\ntwo different algebraic direct limits. P56 depends on accepted P55D.\n\nP60 may run independently of Lane H after P51 and P50U. It is optional Lane-G\nstrengthening and must use P50U's literal ultraweak-normal corner state. It may\nassume an explicitly named countable comparison family for the full corner,\nbut it may not infer a global weight from fullness alone or conceal the weight,\nnormality, faithfulness, traciality, or semifiniteness laws in an axiom.\n\nAmendment, 2026-08-08: P60 compiled and its conditional weight-series,\ntraciality, faithfulness, corner restriction, and finite-compression results\nare preserved, but P60 is not accepted as the optional global-weight theorem.\nThe closeout's P51 provenance objection was stale: P51 is accepted in\n`reviews/P51-full-finite-corner-central-exclusion-recovery.md`. The genuine\nremaining gap is standard semifiniteness on the positive cone. P60R may revise\nthe P60 candidate in place, but must prove that for each nonzero positive\n`x ∈ M` there is a nonzero positive `y ≤ x` of finite weight. It must construct\nthe required positive square-root/factorization argument from Mathlib or\nlocal proved C-star theory; that factorization may not be a new hypothesis.\n\n--- packet ---\n# P55B — coherent source-limit to UHF bridge\n\n## Context declaration\n\n- **Infrastructure only:** identify the algebraic source assembled in P53 with\n  the dyadic finite-coordinate system assembled from P55A. No regional C-star\n  or manuscript theorem is completed here.\n\n## Plan alignment\n\n- **Package and lane:** `P55B`; Lane `H`.\n- **Predecessors:** `P53`, `P55A`, both integrated and locally audited before\n  submission.\n- **Gate discharged:** prove finite-stage coherence and the resulting\n  algebraic direct-limit equivalence, including separate finite and infinite\n  coordinate-index branches.\n- **Forbidden downstream claims:** no operator-range completion, regional\n  C-star alpha, state identity, GNS tensor split, factor classification, or\n  trace/weight conclusion.\n\nRead `PLAN.md` and `work/TWO-LANE-FORMALIZATION-DECISION.md` before editing.\n\n## Mathematical target\n\nCreate only `AristotleCandidates/LocalHyperbolicSourceUHFBridge.lean`.\n\nFirst construct coherent finite orderings of the nested finite coordinate\nblocks `A.Coord n` (or an equivalent finite-set-indexed dyadic system) and\nprove that the P55A stage maps commute with the P53 source connecting maps.\nDo not assume the commuting square. Define the resulting coordinate-dyadic\ndirect limit and construct\n\n`A.sourceToCoordinateDyadic :\n  A.SourceLimit ≃⋆ₐ[ℂ] A.CoordinateDyadicLimit`.\n\nThen prove both mathematically distinct endpoint statements:\n\n1. if `I` is finite, the exhaustion reaches a terminal coordinate block and\n   the source limit is star-equivalent to `QubitTensorPower (Nat.card I)`;\n2. if `I` is infinite, the stage cardinalities are cofinal in `Nat`, and the\n   coordinate-dyadic limit is star-equivalent to `QubitUHFAlgebra`.\n\nExport the composite infinite-branch equivalence as\n`A.sourceUHFEquiv : A.SourceLimit ≃⋆ₐ[ℂ] QubitUHFAlgebra` under the exact\n`Infinite I` hypothesis, and an explicitly named finite-branch equivalence.\nProve formulas on every canonical stage image and uniqueness from those\nformulas.\n\n## Auxiliary assumptions\n\nThe P52 exhaustion and P53 `stage_surjective` are available. Do not assume a\ncoherent enumeration, a commuting square, cofinality, or a direct-limit\nequivalence unless a genuine obstruction in pinned Mathlib makes construction\nimpossible. In that event stop at the smallest proved theorem, name the exact\nmissing lemma/API, and do not package the desired equivalence as a field.\n\n## Files and imports\n\nCreate only `AristotleCandidates/LocalHyperbolicSourceUHFBridge.lean`; import\nP53, P55A, and `Formalization.DyadicTensorTower`. Do not edit predecessors.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- `lake build AristotleCandidates.LocalHyperbolicSourceUHFBridge` passes.\n- The coherence squares and finite/infinite branch hypotheses are explicit.\n- No `sorry`, `admit`, new axiom, supplied coherent family, or supplied\n  direct-limit equivalence is introduced.\n- The response reports exact declarations, commands, assumptions, and any\n  genuine blocked boundary without making downstream claims.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
