tibility equations.  The\n  concrete finite-support quadratic phase is now independently formalized;\n  relating it to the actual regional stabilizer convention remains separate.\n- QPR-001 — the explicit ZMod 4 finite-support quadratic refinement has its\n  polarization and diagonal identities fully checked.  Its discrepancy pairing\n  is additive in both words, symmetric for a symmetric discrepancy, and has\n  additive order two.  These facts instantiate the cross-algebra Pauli-word\n  multiplication and involution certificates and, with a supplied word-basis\n  linear equivalence, a `StarAlgEquiv`.\n- QPT-001 — the concrete finite-support phase theorem now composes that\n  `StarAlgEquiv` with the finite-pure times qubit-UHF trace transport: whenever\n  the regional Pauli-word exponents, involution phases, and word-basis map are\n  supplied, Lean constructs both the star-algebra equivalence and its induced\n  algebraic tracial state with the elementary-tensor product formula.  The\n  Pauli-word interface has been weakened from `Ring` to `Semiring`, the exact\n  structure carried by the concrete algebraic UHF direct limit.\n- PTO-001 — two isometries whose range projections sum to the identity rule\n  out even an algebraic unital cyclic trace.  This is the checked obstruction\n  behind the infinite-pure-sector case; the tracial-state theorem is therefore\n  deliberately limited to a finite pure matrix factor.\n- ALT-001 — compatible finite-stage `StarAlgEquiv`s and compatible target\n  algebraic tracial states induce a source-side algebraic tracial state on the\n  corresponding quasi-local direct limit.  The theorem evaluates it exactly\n  on every finite-stage representative.  The concrete finite-pure UHF trace\n  now has the matching finite-stage elementary-tensor formula.\n- FQP-001 — every finite stage of the dyadic qubit tower now has an explicit\n  ordered Pauli-word `StarSystem` and a complex Pauli-word basis.  The\n  identity-qubit embeddings preserve its words, basis vectors, multiplication\n  multipliers, and star multipliers under coherent label maps.  Thus the UHF\n  target-side finite-stage word hypotheses are no longer abstract assumptions;\n  assembling them into one global target word system remains open.\n- PMS-001 — for every Boolean sequence specifying whether each newly adjoined\n  qubit is pure or maximally mixed, the corresponding finite product\n  functionals are algebraic states, are compatible with all dyadic embeddings,\n  and induce an algebraic state on the UHF direct limit.  Their values on every\n  finite Pauli word are proved recursively: pure coordinates permit only zero\n  X exponent, while mixed coordinates permit only the identity word.  The\n  all-mixed specialization is proved equal to the previously checked UHF\n  tracial state.  Lean also proves that even the one-qubit pure specialization\n  is not cyclic and hence not an algebraic tracial state.\n- PTR-001 — this nontraciality is now proved at arbitrary finite and\n  direct-limit coordinates: if any Boolean coordinate is pure, explicit\n  matrix units witness a failure of cyclicity.  Consequently the algebraic\n  UHF product state is tracial if and only if every coordinate is maximally\n  mixed, in which case it is the checked UHF trace.\n- CBL-001 — finite-stage star-algebra equivalences need not be assumed\n  coherent on every algebra element: if the source connecting maps, target\n  vectors, and coordinate maps agree on a specified source basis, Lean proves\n  the full commuting square by linear-basis extensionality.\n- CPS-001 — a phase-corrected finite coordinate system now has a concrete\n  direct-limit state interface.  Coherent source basis transport, phases, and\n  finite Pauli labels imply full-stage equivalence coherence and hence a\n  star-algebra equivalence to the algebraic qubit-UHF direct limit; the induced\n  source state evaluates a basis word as its phase times the pure/mixed Pauli\n  selection indicator.  The all-mixed specialization pulls the UHF trace back\n  to a source algebraic tracial state; more generally its pure/mixed pullback\n  is tracial exactly when every coordinate is mixed.  Constructing the\n  regional inputs remains open.\n- ACS-001 — if supplied finite-stage regional data identify selected target\n  Z-coordinates with the actual source stabilizer words, Lean derives the\n  exact phase-calibrated stabilizer expectation formula on every source basis word.\n  The stronger form states that hypothesis as literal membership in the\n  selected-Z submodule of an adapted coordinate basis.  Thus the remaining\n  geometric work is isolated to constructing and coherently transporting that\n  coordinate data from a separately supplied finite-coordinate realization,\n  rather than to a hidden infinite-algebra assumption. The manuscript does not\n  presently supply that realization; see `SOURCE-CONTRACT.md`.\n- ALS-001 — compatible finite-stage star-algebra equivalences transport\n  compatible algebraic states (not only tracial states) to a quasi-local\n  algebraic direct limit.  This is the exact state-level interface required by\n  a coherent regional stabilizer-coordinate construction.\n- WBE-001 — if Pauli words form a complex linear basis, checking a\n  complex-linear map on every pair of basis words proves multiplicativity on\n  all finite sums.  The corresponding conjugate-linear basis argument proves\n  star preservation; a bijective unital map satisfying both checks is packaged\n  as a star-algebra equivalence.\n- ALC-001 — a compatible family of finite-stage star-algebra maps induces a\n  star-algebra map from the algebraic directed limit.  Compatible finite-stage\n  star-algebra equivalences induce a star-algebra equivalence of the two\n  algebraic limits.  The C-star norm extension remains open.\n- CSE-001 — once a source and target are supplied as complex C-star algebras,\n  Lean proves that every complex `StarAlgEquiv` is isometric and therefore\n  continuous with continuous inverse.  A continuous target functional pulls\n  back continuously along it.  This does not construct C-star norms or\n  completions for the algebraic direct-limit models.\n- CCF-001 — the pinned Mathlib supports the finite dyadic stages as genuine\n  C-star algebras and supports closure/minimality once an ambient C-star\n  algebra is supplied.  It does not provide the C-star inductive-limit\n  construction for the algebraic dyadic limit; this is recorded as an\n  explicit missing API rather than hidden behind an axiom.\n- NMC-001 — supplied finite C-star realizations of the coherent coordinate\n  maps are isometric and continuous, and the commuting inclusion squares\n  preserve the norm estimates.  The resulting dense-subalgebra estimate is\n  exactly the analytic input needed before extending the algebraic map to a\n  completion; no completion is constructed here.\n- BMC-001 — for a star subalgebra of bounded operators on a Hilbert space,\n  Lean now constructs the algebraic bicommutant as a concrete\n  `VonNeumannAlgebra`, with monotonicity, minimality, membership, and\n  idempotence lemmas.  The analytic strong/weak double-commutant theorem is\n  still explicitly absent from the pinned Mathlib and remains separate.\n- CCC-001 — from an explicitly supplied isometric star representation of a\n  pre-C-star algebra into bounded operators, Lean constructs the closed\n  operator-range C-star algebra, its isometric dense embedding, and the\n  uniqueness equivalence between two such concrete completions.  The faithful\n  operator representation of the project-specific algebraic limit is still a\n  separate obligation.\n\n## The exact theorem still to prove\n\nThe Overleaf short-range theorem asserts a regional von Neumann algebra\nisomorphism to a type-I factor tensor a hyperfinite type-II1 factor.  It is\nnot yet formalized as a theorem because the supplied manuscript proof leaves\nthe following essential premises open:\n\n1. a finite-support adapted symplectic coordinate map whose finite-stage\n   source bases, phase correction, and target Pauli labels are coherent along\n   an exhaustion;\n2. identification of the actual regional Pauli multiplier and involution\n   exponents with the finite-support coordinate discrepancy, followed by\n   calibration to the actual stabilizer character;\n3. the induced quasi-local C-star isomorphism;\n4. factorization of the regional state into pure and normalized-tracial\n   coordinate states; and\n5. a normal/spatial extension to the respective bicommutants.\n\nThe current pinned mathlib version includes preliminary abstract and concrete\nvon Neumann-algebra definitions, but lacks a finished API for infinite von\nNeumann tensor products, normal states/traces, hyperfiniteness, and factor\nclassification.  The project therefore does not introduce any axiom for the\ntarget theorem.\n\n## Last verification\n\n```text\nlake build\nlake build Formalization.AlgebraicLimitStateTransport Formalization.QubitMatrixState Formalization.FinitePureMixedQubitState Formalization\nlake build Formalization.TraceTransport Formalization\nlake build Formalization.CoherentBasisEquiv Formalization.CoherentPhaseQubitState Formalization\nlake build Formalization.PureCoordinateNotTracial Formalization\nlake build Formalization.AdaptedStabilizerSubspace Formalization\nlake build Formalization.FiniteQubitPauliSelection Formalization.CoherentPhaseQubitState Formalization\nlake build Formalization.CStarEquivExtension Formalization\nlake build AristotleCandidates.CStarInductiveLimitFeasibility AristotleCandidates.FiniteCoordinateMapNormControl\nlake env lean /tmp/stabilizer_hyperfinite_axioms_run4.lean\npdflatex -interaction=nonstopmode -halt-on-error .../001-tensor-product-trace.tex\n```\n\nLean reports only `propext`, `Classical.choice`, and `Quot.sound` for the\nchecked tensor-amplification, concrete dyadic direct-limit trace,\nfinite-support quadratic-phase, induced-trace, finite-qubit Pauli-word,\npure/mixed product-state, basis-level coherence, phase-corrected direct-limit\nequivalence/state transport, and properly-infinite trace-obstruction theorems.\nNo source theorem contains `sorry`, `admit`, or a user-declared axiom.  The\nblueprint build output is kept under `/tmp`, not in this source project.\n\n--- P53 closeout ---\n# P53 closeout review — local-hyperbolic algebraic alpha\n\n## Decision\n\n**Status: proved at the stated conditional Lane-H scope; queue may advance.**\n\nThe completed Aristotle project for task\n`11e84c2b-b0a0-420f-ac80-d38a8a5695bb` was downloaded to\n`aristotle_responses/P53-local-hyperbolic-algebraic-alpha.tar.gz`\n(SHA-256\n`89df64accdc83453c13fe7a5a9c6080b80811a3df44947576b0d9e342a100a4f`)\nand extracted, without a build, update, or dependency fetch, under\n`aristotle_responses/P53-quarantine/`. Only the packet-authorized module\n`AristotleCandidates/LocalHyperbolicAlgebraicAlpha.lean` was integrated into\nthe live project. Its quarantine and live SHA-256 values agree:\n`797dd652c0cef03fd6481aee5331446fdad4dba7f4db9f310bda6d6b76efcd1b`.\nThe archive, extraction, and `ARISTOTLE_SUMMARY.md` remain raw response\nrecords; no other candidate module was copied.\n\n## Exact declarations and assumptions\n\nThe module defines the concrete finite twisted-Pauli-word algebra\n`pauliAlgebra`, its word basis `pauliWordBasis`, the coordinate pairing\n`coordPairing`, and `AlphaData`. Under `AlphaData A`, the load-bearing\ndeclarations are:\n\n- `stageLabelMap_bijective`: every finite-stage label map is a bijection;\n- `stage_mulCompatible` and `stage_starCompatible`: the explicitly defined\n  quadratic phase satisfies the word multiplication and involution equations;\n- `stage`: a constructed `FiniteAdaptedCoordinateStarData`, with no supplied\n  finite-stage `StarAlgEquiv` field;\n- `directedFamily`: the coherent finite-stage system;\n- `alpha`: the resulting algebraic direct-limit `StarAlgEquiv`;\n- `alpha_word`, `alpha_zWord`, `alpha_xWord`, `alpha_symm_word`, and\n  `existsUnique_alpha`: the phase-calibrated word and inverse formulas and\n  uniqueness; and\n- `standardAlphaData`: a tautological non-vacuity witness on `Nat`.\n\nThe conditional premises are explicit fields of `AlphaData`:\n\n1. P52's `LocalHyperbolicFamily.indep` and `LatticeExhaustion` data;\n2. `[LinearOrder I]`, used solely for the quadratic-phase ordering convention;\n3. `symplectic`, equality of the antisymmetrized source and target Pauli\n   pairings; and\n4. `stage_surjective`, onto-ness of each finite source-label block onto its\n   regional target-label block.\n\nP52 already proves injectivity and inclusion coherence. P53 derives stage\nbijectivity by combining that proof with `stage_surjective`; it does not hide\nstage equivalences, phase calibration, or whole-stage coherence in fields.\nThe local `symplectic` and `stage_surjective` conditions are additional\nauxiliary assumptions, not consequences established from the manuscript in\nthis repository.\n\n## Acceptance review\n\n| Classification | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| proved | From the named P52 data plus `symplectic` and `stage_surjective`, P53 constructs the finite twisted Pauli algebras, phase-calibrated finite-stage star equivalences, commuting directed system, and algebraic direct-limit star equivalence `alpha`. |\n| partial | The manuscript specialization is conditional: the repository does not construct the actual regional symplectic-coordinate realization or prove the stage-surjectivity premise from the cited manuscript clauses. The formula on generators is phase-calibrated, not an unphased literal equality. |\n| blocked | No obstruction blocks this algebraic gate. The next gates—concrete C-star realization/extension, product-state identity, GNS spatial tensor splitting, factorhood, and trace/weight classification—remain P54--P59 work. |\n| failed | None. |\n\nThe packet's mathematical target is met at its stated conditional scope. The\nalternative route builds a project-local finite twisted-word algebra rather\nthan assuming stage equivalences. This adds precisely `symplectic` and\n`stage_surjective` as premises; it does not weaken the requested conclusion.\n\n## Plan alignment\n\n- **Package and lane:** P53, Lane H.\n- **Predecessors:** P52 is integrated, compiled, and locally audited in\n  `reviews/P52-coherent-local-hyperbolic-coordinates-closeout.md`. The module\n  imports P52 plus checked phase/coherence/direct-limit infrastructure; it\n  imports no later P54--P61 package.\n- **Permitted gate:** discharged: constructed phase-calibrated finite-stage\n  star equivalences, their coherent algebraic direct-limit equivalence, and\n  the direct-limit `alpha` word formulas.\n- **Forbidden downstream claims:** respected. The module explicitly makes no\n  C-star completion, state identity, GNS tensor split, spatial tensor-product,\n  factorhood, trace, or weight theorem, and no such declaration occurs.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `lake build AristotleCandidates/LocalHyperbolicAlgebraicAlpha.lean` — passed\n  in the live project (8045 jobs); no build ran in quarantine.\n- `lake build` — passed in the live project.\n- `lake env lean /dev/stdin` with `#print axioms` for\n  `stageLabelMap_bijective`, `stage_mulCompatible`, `stage_starCompatible`,\n  `directedFamily`, `alpha`, `alpha_word`, `alpha_zWord`, `alpha_xWord`,\n  `existsUnique_alpha`, and `standardAlphaData` — each reports only\n  `propext`, `Classical.choice`, and `Quot.sound`.\n- Placeholder scan across the candidate and its direct P52/phase/direct-limit\n  imports — no `sorry`, `admit`, user `axiom`, `opaque`, `unsafe`,\n  `implemented_by`, or `native_decide` occurrence.\n- Quarantine/live SHA-256 comparison and `git diff --check` — passed.\n\n## Adversarial review\n\nNo acceptance-blocking finding. The review checked that finite-stage\nsurjectivity is exposed rather than inferred from P52, that symmetry of the\ndiscrepancy is obtained only from the named symplectic premise, that the\nquadratic phase is used in both multiplication and star compatibility, and\nthat `alpha_zWord`/`alpha_xWord` retain the phase. Compilation validates the\nformal conditional construction; it does not establish the manuscript's\ngeometric realization or any later analytic/operator-algebraic statement.\n\n## Cleanup and worktree state\n\nKept intentionally: the integrated P53 candidate, its response archive,\nquarantine extraction, and this review. Pre-existing untracked P49/P49A/P49B\ncandidate and review files remain untouched. No manuscript file was changed;\nno commit, push, dependency update, archive build, or dependency fetch was\nperformed.\n\n--- P55A closeout ---\n# P55A closeout review — local-hyperbolic finite-stage UHF bridge\n\n## Decision\n\n**Status: proved at the stated infrastructure-only Lane-H scope; queue may\nadvance.**\n\nThe terminal status for Aristotle task\n`2e89017e-ccab-47c2-bd66-ca42164fd972` is `COMPLETE` in\n`history/logs/20260808T161409Z-1ac3c887-tasks.log`.\nIts exact archive\n`aristotle_responses/P55A-local-hyperbolic-finite-stage-uhf-bridge-1ac3c887-2e89017e.tar.gz`\nwas extracted only to\n`aristotle_responses/P55A-local-hyperbolic-finite-stage-uhf-bridge-1ac3c887-2e89017e-quarantine/`.\nNo build, update, or dependency fetch was run in that dependency-free\nsnapshot.  Only the packet-authorized candidate\n`AristotleCandidates/LocalHyperbolicFiniteStageUHFBridge.lean` was\nintegrated into the live project.  Its live and quarantine SHA-256 values\nagree:\n\n```text\n42b18ef984b2046a4004ae64e8e79a0df7454e0c122b8d9722145bc6e2d28b3a\n```\n\nNo raw response record was integrated: the packet authorizes only the\ncandidate module.  The archive and quarantine extraction are retained as raw\nevidence.\n\n## Exact declarations and assumptions\n\nThe new module imports the accepted P53 module\n`AristotleCandidates.LocalHyperbolicAlgebraicAlpha` and\n`Formalization.DyadicTensorTower`; their archived versions are\nbyte-identical to the live versions.  It constructs, rather than receives as\na field:\n\n- `UHFBridge.qubitMatrixEquiv k :\n  QubitTensorPower k ≃⋆ₐ[ℂ] Matrix (Reg (Fin k)) (Reg (Fin k)) ℂ`;\n- recursive dyadic words `qubitX`, `qubitZ`, and\n  `qubitWord k a b := qubitX k a * qubitZ k b`;\n- `AlphaData.sourceStageMatrixEquiv n e`, obtained from P53's\n  `pauliWordBasis`, the explicitly proved matrix-word basis\n  `stdWordBasis`, and the supplied enumeration\n  `e : A.Coord n ≃ Fin k`; and\n- the packet target\n\n  ```lean\n  A.sourceStageUHFEquiv n e :\n    pauliAlgebra (A.sourceForm n) ≃⋆ₐ[ℂ] QubitTensorPower k\n  ```\n\n  defined by transport through the constructed register-matrix equivalence.\n\nThe exact word and generator formulae are:\n\n```lean\nA.sourceStageUHFEquiv n e (pauliWord (A.sourceForm n) v) =\n  qubitWord k (A.enumRepr n e v).1 (A.enumRepr n e v).2\n\nA.sourceStageUHFEquiv n e\n    (pauliWord (A.sourceForm n) ((A.stageCoordinates n).z i)) =\n  qubitZ k (Pi.single (e i) 1)\n\nA.sourceStageUHFEquiv n e\n    (pauliWord (A.sourceForm n) ((A.stageCoordinates n).x i)) =\n  qubitX k (Pi.single (e i) 1)\n```\n\nThey are exported as `sourceStageUHFEquiv_word`,\n`sourceStageUHFEquiv_zGenerator`, and\n`sourceStageUHFEquiv_xGenerator`, together with\n`sourceStageUHFEquiv_bijective`,\n`sourceStageUHFEquivDefault` at `Nat.card (A.Coord n)`, and\n`norm_sourceStageUHFEquiv`,\n`norm_sourceStageMatrixEquiv`, and\n`isometry_sourceStageMatrixEquiv`.\n\nThe convention check is explicit.  The ordered word is `X^a Z^b`; its\nmultiplication sign is `(-1)^(b dot a')`, its star sign is\n`(-1)^(a dot b)`, and\n`i^(a dot b) X^a Z^b` is proved self-adjoint.  Both coordinate-generator\nimages have trivial fourth-root phase because their respective exponent\npairings vanish.  The recursive tensor convention puts coordinate zero in the\nouter matrix factor through `regSuccEquiv`; no unproved permutation is used.\n\nThere are no new mathematical premises.  The bridge inherits exactly P53's\n`AlphaData` data: a P52 locally supported hyperbolic family and exhaustion,\nplus the explicitly named auxiliary fields `symplectic` and\n`stage_surjective`.  The finite coordinate enumeration is constructed with\n`Finite.equivFin`; classical choice is not a supplied hypothesis.  Since\n`QubitTensorPower k` has no native normed additive structure in the pinned\nAPI, the candidate defines `qubitOpNorm` through the proved register-matrix\nmodel and states the distance-form isometry in that matrix model.  This is an\nexplicit norm-control route, not a hidden C-star completion premise.\n\n## Acceptance review\n\n| Classification | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| proved | From every explicit enumeration `e`, the finite P53 source Pauli algebra is star-isomorphic to the corresponding recursive `k`-qubit dyadic stage; the word, X/Z-generator, multiplication, star, bijectivity, and induced norm statements are proved. |\n| partial | This is infrastructure only.  It does not construct the manuscript's actual coordinate realization; it inherits P53's named `AlphaData` assumptions and does not identify any direct limit. |\n| blocked | None at the P55A gate. |\n| failed | None. |\n\nThe packet's mathematical target is met exactly at its stated scope.  The\nsupporting matrix route is not a weakened target: it constructs an explicit\nstar equivalence between the recursive dyadic stage and its finite register\nmatrix model before transporting the explicitly constructed Pauli-word map.\nNo added premise or alternate conditional conclusion was introduced.\n\n## Plan alignment\n\n- **Package and lane:** P55A, Lane H, as declared in the packet and the active\n  plan.\n- **Predecessors:** P53 only.  Its accepted, locally compiled, semantically\n  audited closeout is\n  `reviews/P53-local-hyperbolic-algebraic-alpha-closeout.md`.  P55A imports\n  that live module and standard checked dyadic infrastructure; it does not\n  use P55B--P55D or an unaccepted remote artifact.\n- **Permitted gate:** discharged: constructed finite-stage Pauli-to-dyadic\n  star equivalences, explicit generator/phase formulae, and norm control.\n- **Forbidden downstream claims:** respected.  No declaration identifies a\n  direct limit, constructs a C-star completion or regional alpha, proves a\n  state identity or GNS split, calls an algebra a factor, or gives a\n  trace/weight conclusion.\n\nNo manuscript source clause is represented by this infrastructure-only\npacket.  In particular, it does not promote the still-unformalized\nshort-range regional-algebra theorem or its analytic tensor-product steps.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `lake build AristotleCandidates.LocalHyperbolicFiniteStageUHFBridge` —\n  passed in the live project (`8050/8050` jobs).\n- `lake build` — passed in the live project.\n- `lake env lean /dev/stdin` importing the live candidate and printing the\n  axioms of `sourceStageUHFEquiv`,\n  `sourceStageUHFEquiv_zGenerator`,\n  `sourceStageUHFEquiv_xGenerator`,\n  `sourceStageUHFEquiv_bijective`, and\n  `norm_sourceStageUHFEquiv` — each reports only `propext`,\n  `Classical.choice`, and `Quot.sound`.\n- Placeholder scan of the candidate and its direct P53/dyadic imports — no\n  `sorry`, `admit`, user `axiom`, `opaque`, `unsafe`,\n  `implemented_by`, or `native_decide` occurrence.\n- Quarantine/live SHA-256 comparison and\n  `git diff --check -- AristotleCandidates/LocalHyperbolicFiniteStageUHFBridge.lean`\n  — passed.\n\n## Adversarial review\n\nNo acceptance-blocking finding.  The review checked the multiplication order\nand all three convention-sensitive signs, the zero-coordinate and default\nfinite-enumeration cases, that the basis transport proves rather than assumes\nthe stage equivalence, and that the custom dyadic norm is explicitly defined\nthrough the constructed matrix model.  It also checked the packet's scope\nagainst P55B--P59: no forbidden downstream statement is present.  Compilation\nand axiom reports validate this finite conditional infrastructure only; they\ndo not valid