{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"qroot='aristotle_responses/P55B-local-hyperbolic-source-uhf-bridge-809ad1ae-5b40a5f6-quarantine/aristotle-stabilizer_two_lane_p55b-r95x55if_aristotle'\nprintf '%s\\\\n' '--- candidate hashes ---'\nsha256sum AristotleCandidates/LocalHyperbolicSourceUHFBridge.lean \\\"\"'$qroot/AristotleCandidates/LocalHyperbolicSourceUHFBridge.lean\"\nprintf '\"'%s\\\\n' '--- candidate diff ---'\ndiff -u AristotleCandidates/LocalHyperbolicSourceUHFBridge.lean \\\"\"'$qroot/AristotleCandidates/LocalHyperbolicSourceUHFBridge.lean\" || true\nprintf '\"'%s\\\\n' '--- candidate source ---'\nsed -n '1,420p' \\\"\"'$qroot/AristotleCandidates/LocalHyperbolicSourceUHFBridge.lean\"\nprintf '\"'%s\\\\n' '--- live work status/handoff ---'\nrg --files work | sort | xargs -r -n1 sh -c 'printf \\\"--- %s ---\\\\\\\\n\\\" \\\"\"'$0\"; sed -n \"1,240p\" \"$0\"'\"'\"","aggregated_output":"--- candidate hashes ---\nsha256sum: AristotleCandidates/LocalHyperbolicSourceUHFBridge.lean: No such file or directory\nf754604e0c6a1f870158f81cda06223a86364d0a461816b9e9e5e7c9f7261cad  aristotle_responses/P55B-local-hyperbolic-source-uhf-bridge-809ad1ae-5b40a5f6-quarantine/aristotle-stabilizer_two_lane_p55b-r95x55if_aristotle/AristotleCandidates/LocalHyperbolicSourceUHFBridge.lean\n--- candidate diff ---\ndiff: AristotleCandidates/LocalHyperbolicSourceUHFBridge.lean: No such file or directory\n--- candidate source ---\nimport AristotleCandidates.LocalHyperbolicFiniteStageUHFBridge\nimport Formalization.DyadicTensorTower\n\n/-!\n# P55B — the coherent source-limit to UHF bridge\n\n**Context declaration: infrastructure only.**  No manuscript claim is asserted\nin this module.  It identifies the algebraic source direct limit assembled in\nP53 (`AristotleCandidates.LocalHyperbolicAlgebraicAlpha`) with the dyadic\nfinite-coordinate system assembled from the finite-stage bridges of P55A\n(`AristotleCandidates.LocalHyperbolicFiniteStageUHFBridge`).\n\n## Plan alignment\n\n* Package `P55B`, lane `H`; predecessors `P53` and `P55A`.\n* Gate: prove finite-stage coherence of the P55A stage maps with the P53 source\n  connecting maps, construct the coordinate-dyadic direct limit and its\n  star-equivalence with the P53 source limit, and prove the two endpoint\n  statements (terminal finite block, cofinal infinite exhaustion) separately.\n* No operator-range completion, regional C⋆ alpha, state identity, GNS tensor\n  split, factor classification, or trace/weight conclusion is claimed here.\n\n## What is constructed\n\n1. A **coherent enumeration** of the nested finite coordinate blocks: each\n   block `A.Coord n` is enumerated by `Fin (A.stageCard n)` so that passing\n   from stage `n` to stage `m ≥ n` shifts every old coordinate by exactly\n   `A.stageCard m - A.stageCard n` positions.  This is *constructed* from the\n   P52 exhaustion (through the birth stage of a coordinate and the given linear\n   order on `I`), not assumed.\n2. The **commuting squares**: the P55A stage equivalences intertwine the P53\n   source connecting maps with the dyadic tower maps\n   (`stageUHFEquiv_sourceConnecting`).  This is proved, not assumed.\n3. The **coordinate-dyadic direct limit** `A.CoordinateDyadicLimit` and the\n   star equivalence `A.sourceToCoordinateDyadic`, with its stage formula and\n   uniqueness.\n4. The **finite branch**: if `I` is finite the exhaustion has a terminal\n   coordinate block and `A.sourceFiniteEquiv` identifies the source limit with\n   `QubitTensorPower (Nat.card I)`.\n5. The **infinite branch**: if `I` is infinite the stage cardinalities are\n   cofinal in `ℕ`, the coordinate-dyadic limit is the qubit UHF algebra, and\n   `A.sourceUHFEquiv : A.SourceLimit ≃⋆ₐ[ℂ] QubitUHFAlgebra`.\n-/\n\nnamespace StabilizerHyperfinite\n\nnamespace UHFBridge\n\nopen LocalHyperbolicAlpha\n\n/-! ## Padding of finite registers along the dyadic tower\n\nThe dyadic connecting map `qubitTensorPowerMap k k'` adjoins new qubits on the\n*left* of a register, so on exponent vectors it is the padding that places the\nold `k`-qubit register in the last `k` positions of a `k'`-qubit register. -/\n\n/-- Pad an exponent vector of a `k`-qubit register into a `k'`-qubit register,\nplacing the old register in the last `k` positions. -/\ndef padReg (k k' : ℕ) (a : Reg (Fin k)) : Reg (Fin k') :=\n  fun j => if h : k' ≤ (j : ℕ) + k then a ⟨(j : ℕ) + k - k', by have := j.isLt; omega⟩ else 0\n\ntheorem padReg_self (k : ℕ) (a : Reg (Fin k)) : padReg k k a = a := by\n  funext j\n  rw [padReg, dif_pos (by omega)]\n  congr 1\n  exact Fin.ext (by simp)\n\ntheorem padReg_succ {k k' : ℕ} (h : k ≤ k') (a : Reg (Fin k)) :\n    padReg k (k' + 1) a = Fin.cons 0 (padReg k k' a) := by\n  funext j\n  induction j using Fin.cases with\n  | zero => rw [padReg, dif_neg (by simp; omega)]; rfl\n  | succ i =>\n      rw [Fin.cons_succ, padReg, padReg]\n      by_cases hc : k' ≤ (i : ℕ) + k\n      · rw [dif_pos (by rw [Fin.val_succ]; omega), dif_pos hc]\n        congr 1\n        refine Fin.ext ?_\n        simp only [Fin.val_succ]\n        omega\n      · rw [dif_neg (by rw [Fin.val_succ]; omega), dif_neg hc]\n\n/-- The value of a padded exponent vector at a position coming from the old\nregister. -/\ntheorem padReg_apply_of_le {k k' : ℕ} (a : Reg (Fin k)) (j : Fin k') (i : Fin k)\n    (hij : (j : ℕ) + k = k' + (i : ℕ)) : padReg k k' a j = a i := by\n  rw [padReg, dif_pos (by omega)]\n  congr 1\n  exact Fin.ext (by simp; omega)\n\n/-- The value of a padded exponent vector at a genuinely new position. -/\ntheorem padReg_apply_of_lt {k k' : ℕ} (a : Reg (Fin k)) (j : Fin k')\n    (hj : (j : ℕ) + k < k') : padReg k k' a j = 0 := by\n  rw [padReg, dif_neg (by omega)]\n\ntheorem succEmbedding_qubitX (k : ℕ) (a : Reg (Fin k)) :\n    qubitTensorPowerSuccEmbedding k (qubitX k a) = qubitX (k + 1) (Fin.cons 0 a) := by\n  have h1 : qubitX (k + 1) (Fin.cons 0 a) =\n      (Matrix.of fun r c : Fin 2 =>\n        if bitEquiv r = (Fin.cons (0 : PauliBit) a : Reg (Fin (k + 1))) 0 + bitEquiv c\n        then qubitX k (Fin.tail (Fin.cons (0 : PauliBit) a : Reg (Fin (k + 1)))) else 0 :\n          Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) (QubitTensorPower k)) := rfl\n  rw [h1]\n  show Matrix.scalar (Fin 2) (qubitX k a) = _\n  ext r c\n  rw [Fin.cons_zero, Fin.tail_cons]\n  show (Matrix.diagonal (fun _ => qubitX k a)) r c =\n    if bitEquiv r = 0 + bitEquiv c then qubitX k a else 0\n  rw [Matrix.diagonal_apply, zero_add]\n  by_cases h : r = c\n  · rw [if_pos h, if_pos (by rw [h])]\n  · rw [if_neg h, if_neg (fun hh => h (bitEquiv.injective hh))]\n\ntheorem succEmbedding_qubitZ (k : ℕ) (b : Reg (Fin k)) :\n    qubitTensorPowerSuccEmbedding k (qubitZ k b) = qubitZ (k + 1) (Fin.cons 0 b) := by\n  have h1 : qubitZ (k + 1) (Fin.cons 0 b) =\n      (Matrix.of fun r c : Fin 2 =>\n        if r = c then pauliSign ((Fin.cons (0 : PauliBit) b : Reg (Fin (k + 1))) 0 * bitEquiv c) •\n          qubitZ k (Fin.tail (Fin.cons (0 : PauliBit) b : Reg (Fin (k + 1)))) else 0 :\n          Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) (QubitTensorPower k)) := rfl\n  rw [h1]\n  show Matrix.scalar (Fin 2) (qubitZ k b) = _\n  ext r c\n  rw [Fin.cons_zero, Fin.tail_cons]\n  show (Matrix.diagonal (fun _ => qubitZ k b)) r c =\n    if r = c then pauliSign (0 * bitEquiv c) • qubitZ k b else 0\n  rw [Matrix.diagonal_apply, zero_mul, pauliSign_zero, one_smul]\n\ntheorem succEmbedding_qubitWord (k : ℕ) (a b : Reg (Fin k)) :\n    qubitTensorPowerSuccEmbedding k (qubitWord k a b) =\n      qubitWord (k + 1) (Fin.cons 0 a) (Fin.cons 0 b) := by\n  rw [qubitWord, qubitWord, map_mul, succEmbedding_qubitX, succEmbedding_qubitZ]\n\n/-- **The dyadic tower map on standard words**: the canonical inclusion of the\n`k`-qubit stage into the `k'`-qubit stage is the zero-padding of exponent\nvectors. -/\ntheorem qubitTensorPowerMap_qubitWord (k k' : ℕ) (h : k ≤ k') (a b : Reg (Fin k)) :\n    qubitTensorPowerMap k k' h (qubitWord k a b) =\n      qubitWord k' (padReg k k' a) (padReg k k' b) := by\n  induction k', h using Nat.le_induction with\n  | base => rw [qubitTensorPowerMap_self, padReg_self, padReg_self]; rfl\n  | succ m hm ih =>\n      rw [qubitTensorPowerMap_succ k m hm, StarAlgHom.comp_apply, ih,\n        succEmbedding_qubitWord, padReg_succ hm, padReg_succ hm]\n\n/-- The canonical map of a dyadic stage into the qubit UHF algebra. -/\nnoncomputable abbrev qubitUHFOf (k : ℕ) (x : QubitTensorPower k) : QubitUHFAlgebra :=\n  DirectLimit.Module.of ℂ ℕ QubitTensorPower qubitTensorPowerMap k x\n\ntheorem qubitUHFOf_map {k k' : ℕ} (h : k ≤ k') (x : QubitTensorPower k) :\n    qubitUHFOf k' (qubitTensorPowerMap k k' h x) = qubitUHFOf k x :=\n  DirectLimit.Module.of_f (hij := h)\n\n/-- Dyadic stages with the same number of qubits are canonically identified. -/\nnoncomputable def qubitTensorPowerCongr {k k' : ℕ} (h : k = k') :\n    QubitTensorPower k ≃⋆ₐ[ℂ] QubitTensorPower k' := by\n  subst h; exact StarAlgEquiv.refl\n\n@[simp] theorem qubitTensorPowerCongr_refl (k : ℕ) (x : QubitTensorPower k) :\n    qubitTensorPowerCongr (rfl : k = k) x = x := rfl\n\ntheorem qubitTensorPowerCongr_trans {k k' k'' : ℕ} (h : k = k') (h' : k' = k'')\n    (x : QubitTensorPower k) :\n    qubitTensorPowerCongr h' (qubitTensorPowerCongr h x) =\n      qubitTensorPowerCongr (h.trans h') x := by\n  subst h; subst h'; rfl\n\n/-- If no qubit is added, the dyadic tower map is the canonical identification. -/\ntheorem qubitTensorPowerMap_of_eq {k k' : ℕ} (h : k ≤ k') (he : k = k')\n    (x : QubitTensorPower k) :\n    qubitTensorPowerMap k k' h x = qubitTensorPowerCongr he x := by\n  subst he\n  rw [qubitTensorPowerMap_self]\n  rfl\n\ntheorem qubitTensorPowerMap_bijective_of_eq {k k' : ℕ} (h : k ≤ k') (he : k = k') :\n    Function.Bijective (qubitTensorPowerMap k k' h) := by\n  have : ∀ x, qubitTensorPowerMap k k' h x = qubitTensorPowerCongr he x :=\n    qubitTensorPowerMap_of_eq h he\n  rw [show (qubitTensorPowerMap k k' h : QubitTensorPower k → QubitTensorPower k') =\n    (qubitTensorPowerCongr he : QubitTensorPower k → QubitTensorPower k') from funext this]\n  exact (qubitTensorPowerCongr he).bijective\n\nend UHFBridge\n\n/-! ## The coherent enumeration of the nested coordinate blocks -/\n\nnamespace LocalHyperbolicAlpha\n\nnamespace AlphaData\n\nopen CoherentLocalHyperbolic UHFBridge\nopen scoped Classical\n\nvariable {L I : Type*} [LinearOrder I] (A : AlphaData L I)\n\n/-- The first stage of the P52 exhaustion whose coordinate block contains `i`. -/\nnoncomputable def birth (i : I) : ℕ :=\n  Nat.find (A.family.exists_mem_coordinateBlock A.exhaustion i)\n\ntheorem mem_coordinateBlock_birth (i : I) :\n    i ∈ A.family.coordinateBlock A.exhaustion (A.birth i) :=\n  Nat.find_spec (A.family.exists_mem_coordinateBlock A.exhaustion i)\n\ntheorem birth_le_of_mem {i : I} {n : ℕ} (h : i ∈ A.family.coordinateBlock A.exhaustion n) :\n    A.birth i ≤ n :=\n  Nat.find_min' _ h\n\ntheorem mem_coordinateBlock_of_birth_le {i : I} {n : ℕ} (h : A.birth i ≤ n) :\n    i ∈ A.family.coordinateBlock A.exhaustion n :=\n  A.family.coordinateBlock_mono A.exhaustion h (A.mem_coordinateBlock_birth i)\n\n/-- The stage-`n` coordinate block as a finite set of labels. -/\nnoncomputable def blockFinset (n : ℕ) : Finset I := A.family.blockFinset A.exhaustion n\n\n@[simp] theorem mem_blockFinset (n : ℕ) (i : I) :\n    i ∈ A.blockFinset n ↔ i ∈ A.family.coordinateBlock A.exhaustion n :=\n  A.family.mem_blockFinset A.exhaustion n i\n\ntheorem blockFinset_subset {n m : ℕ} (h : n ≤ m) : A.blockFinset n ⊆ A.blockFinset m := by\n  intro i hi\n  rw [mem_blockFinset] at hi ⊢\n  exact A.family.coordinateBlock_mono A.exhaustion h hi\n\n/-- The number of coordinates of the stage-`n` block: the number of qubits of\nthe dyadic stage attached to it. -/\nnoncomputable def stageCard (n : ℕ) : ℕ := (A.blockFinset n).card\n\ntheorem stageCard_mono {n m : ℕ} (h : n ≤ m) : A.stageCard n ≤ A.stageCard m :=\n  Finset.card_le_card (A.blockFinset_subset h)\n\ntheorem card_coord (n : ℕ) : Fintype.card (A.Coord n) = A.stageCard n := by\n  rw [stageCard, blockFinset, CoherentLocalHyperbolic.LocalHyperbolicFamily.blockFinset,\n    Set.Finite.card_toFinset]\n\n/-- The ordering key of a coordinate: its birth stage first, then the linear\norder of the coordinate index type.  Coordinate blocks are exactly the initial\nsegments of this order that the exhaustion produces. -/\nnoncomputable def key (i : I) : ℕ ×ₗ I := toLex (A.birth i, i)\n\ntheorem key_lt_of_birth_lt {i j : I} (h : A.birth i < A.birth j) : A.key i < A.key j :=\n  Prod.Lex.lt_iff.2 (Or.inl h)\n\ntheorem birth_le_of_key_lt {i j : I} (h : A.key i < A.key j) : A.birth i ≤ A.birth j := by\n  rcases Prod.Lex.lt_iff.1 h with h | ⟨h, -⟩\n  · exact le_of_lt h\n  · exact le_of_eq h\n\ntheorem key_injective : Function.Injective A.key := by\n  intro i j h\n  have := congrArg (fun z => (ofLex z).2) h\n  simpa using this\n\n/-- **The position of a coordinate inside its stage block**: the number of block\ncoordinates that are strictly later in the birth-stage ordering.  Coordinates\nborn at a later stage therefore receive the smaller positions, which is the\nconvention forced by the dyadic tower. -/\nnoncomputable def rankIdx (n : ℕ) (i : I) : ℕ :=\n  ((A.blockFinset n).filter (fun j => A.key i < A.key j)).card\n\ntheorem rankIdx_lt {n : ℕ} {i : I} (hi : i ∈ A.blockFinset n) :\n    A.rankIdx n i < A.stageCard n := by\n  refine Finset.card_lt_card ?_\n  refine (Finset.ssubset_iff_of_subset (Finset.filter_subset _ _)).2 ⟨i, hi, ?_⟩\n  simp\n\ntheorem rankIdx_lt_rankIdx {n : ℕ} {i j : I} (hj : j ∈ A.blockFinset n)\n    (hij : A.key i < A.key j) : A.rankIdx n j < A.rankIdx n i := by\n  refine Finset.card_lt_card ?_\n  refine (Finset.ssubset_iff_of_subset ?_).2 ⟨j, ?_, ?_⟩\n  · intro p hp\n    rw [Finset.mem_filter] at hp ⊢\n    exact ⟨hp.1, hij.trans hp.2⟩\n  · rw [Finset.mem_filter]; exact ⟨hj, hij⟩\n  · simp\n\ntheorem rankIdx_injOn {n : ℕ} {i j : I} (hi : i ∈ A.blockFinset n) (hj : j ∈ A.blockFinset n)\n    (h : A.rankIdx n i = A.rankIdx n j) : i = j := by\n  rcases lt_trichotomy (A.key i) (A.key j) with hlt | heq | hgt\n  · have := A.rankIdx_lt_rankIdx hj hlt; omega\n  · exact A.key_injective heq\n  · have := A.rankIdx_lt_rankIdx (i := j) (j := i) hi hgt; omega\n\n/-- **Coherence of the block enumeration.**  Passing from stage `n` to a later\nstage shifts the position of every old coordinate by exactly the number of new\ncoordinates. -/\ntheorem stageCard_add_rankIdx {n m : ℕ} (hnm : n ≤ m) {i : I} (hi : i ∈ A.blockFinset n) :\n    A.stageCard n + A.rankIdx m i = A.stageCard m + A.rankIdx n i := by\n  classical\n  set S := A.blockFinset n with hS\n  set T := A.blockFinset m with hT\n  have hST : S ⊆ T := A.blockFinset_subset hnm\n  have hbi : A.birth i ≤ n := A.birth_le_of_mem ((A.mem_blockFinset n i).1 hi)\n  have hsplit : T.filter (fun j => A.key i < A.key j) =\n      S.filter (fun j => A.key i < A.key j) ∪ (T \\ S).filter (fun j => A.key i < A.key j) := by\n    rw [← Finset.filter_union, Finset.union_sdiff_of_subset hST]\n  have hdisj : Disjoint (S.filter (fun j => A.key i < A.key j))\n      ((T \\ S).filter (fun j => A.key i < A.key j)) :=\n    Finset.disjoint_filter_filter Finset.disjoint_sdiff\n  have hall : (T \\ S).filter (fun j => A.key i < A.key j) = T \\ S := by\n    refine Finset.filter_true_of_mem ?_\n    intro j hj\n    rw [Finset.mem_sdiff] at hj\n    refine A.key_lt_of_birth_lt ?_\n    have hjn : ¬ A.birth j ≤ n := by\n      intro hle\n      exact hj.2 ((A.mem_blockFinset n j).2 (A.mem_coordinateBlock_of_birth_le hle))\n    omega\n  have hcard : A.rankIdx m i = A.rankIdx n i + (T \\ S).card := by\n    rw [rankIdx, rankIdx, ← hS, ← hT, hsplit, Finset.card_union_of_disjoint hdisj, hall]\n  have hcards : (T \\ S).card + S.card = T.card := Finset.card_sdiff_add_card_eq_card hST\n  rw [stageCard, stageCard, ← hS, ← hT, hcard]\n  omega\n\n/-- **The new coordinates occupy the leading positions.**  A coordinate of a\nlater block that is not yet present at stage `n` has position strictly below\nthe number of new coordinates. -/\ntheorem stageCard_add_rankIdx_lt {n m : ℕ} (hnm : n ≤ m) {i : I} (him : i ∈ A.blockFinset m)\n    (hin : i ∉ A.blockFinset n) : A.stageCard n + A.rankIdx m i < A.stageCard m := by\n  classical\n  set S := A.blockFinset n with hS\n  set T := A.blockFinset m with hT\n  have hST : S ⊆ T := A.blockFinset_subset hnm\n  have hbi : ¬ A.birth i ≤ n := by\n    intro hle\n    exact hin ((A.mem_blockFinset n i).2 (A.mem_coordinateBlock_of_birth_le hle))\n  have hsub : T.filter (fun j => A.key i < A.key j) ⊆ (T \\ S).erase i := by\n    intro j hj\n    rw [Finset.mem_filter] at hj\n    rw [Finset.mem_erase, Finset.mem_sdiff]\n    refine ⟨?_, hj.1, ?_⟩\n    · intro hji\n      exact absurd (hji ▸ hj.2) (lt_irrefl _)\n    · intro hjS\n      have h1 : A.birth j ≤ n := A.birth_le_of_mem ((A.mem_blockFinset n j).1 hjS)\n      have h2 := A.birth_le_of_key_lt hj.2\n      omega\n  have h1 : A.rankIdx m i ≤ ((T \\ S).erase i).card := Finset.card_le_card hsub\n  have h2 : ((T \\ S).erase i).card = (T \\ S).card - 1 := Finset.card_erase_of_mem\n    (by rw [Finset.mem_sdiff]; exact ⟨him, hin⟩)\n  have h3 : 0 < (T \\ S).card := Finset.card_pos.2 ⟨i, by rw [Finset.mem_sdiff]; exact ⟨him, hin⟩⟩\n  have hcards : (T \\ S).card + S.card = T.card := Finset.card_sdiff_add_card_eq_card hST\n  rw [stageCard, stageCard, ← hS, ← hT]\n  omega\n\n/-! ### The coherent enumeration of a stage -/\n\ntheorem rankIdx_bijective (n : ℕ) :\n    Function.Bijective\n      (fun i : A.Coord n => (⟨A.rankIdx n (i : I),\n        A.rankIdx_lt ((A.mem_blockFinset n (i : I)).2 i.2)⟩ : Fin (A.stageCard n))) := by\n  rw [Fintype.bijective_iff_injective_and_card]\n  refine ⟨?_, ?_⟩\n  · intro i j hij\n    exact Subtype.ext (A.rankIdx_injOn ((A.mem_blockFinset n (i : I)).2 i.2)\n      ((A.mem_blockFinset n (j : I)).2 j.2) (congrArg Fin.val hij))\n  · rw [A.card_coord n, Fintype.card_fin]\n\n/-- **The constructed coherent enumeration of a stage coordinate block.** -/\nnoncomputable def stageEnum (n : ℕ) : A.Coord n ≃ Fin (A.stageCard n) :=\n  Equiv.ofBijective _ (A.rankIdx_bijective n)\n\n@[simp] theorem stageEnum_val (n : ℕ) (i : A.Coord n) :\n    ((A.stageEnum n i : Fin (A.stageCard n)) : ℕ) = A.rankIdx n (i : I) := rfl\n\n/-- The inclusion of a stage coordinate block into a later one. -/\ndef coordIncl {n m : ℕ} (h : n ≤ m) (i : A.Coord n) : A.Coord m :=\n  ⟨(i : I), A.family.coordinateBlock_mono A.exhaustion h i.2⟩\n\n@[simp] theorem coordIncl_coe {n m : ℕ} (h : n ≤ m) (i : A.Coord n) :\n    ((A.coordIncl h i : A.Coord m) : I) = (i : I) := rfl\n\n/-- **The coherence equation of the constructed enumerations.** -/\ntheorem stageEnum_coherent {n m : ℕ} (h : n ≤ m) (i : A.Coord n) :\n    A.stageCard n + ((A.stageEnum m (A.coordIncl h i) : Fin (A.stageCard m)) : ℕ) =\n      A.stageCard m + ((A.stageEnum n i : Fin (A.stageCard n)) : ℕ) := by\n  rw [stageEnum_val, stageEnum_val, coordIncl_coe]\n  exact A.stageCard_add_rankIdx h ((A.mem_blockFinset n (i : I)).2 i.2)\n\n/-- **The leading positions of a later stage are the new coordinates.** -/\ntheorem stageEnum_lt_of_not_mem {n m : ℕ} (h : n ≤ m) (i : A.Coord m)\n    (hi : (i : I) ∉ A.family.coordinateBlock A.exhaustion n) :\n    A.stageCard n + ((A.stageEnum m i : Fin (A.stageCard m)) : ℕ) < A.stageCard m := by\n  rw [stageEnum_val]\n  exact A.stageCard_add_rankIdx_lt h ((A.mem_blockFinset m (i : I)).2 i.2)\n    (fun hc => hi ((A.mem_blockFinset n (i : I)).1 hc))\n\n/-! ## Exponent coordinates along the source inclusions -/\n\n/-- The basis coefficients of a stage label are the coefficients of the\nunderlying finitely supported coordinate word. -/\ntheorem stageCoordBasis_repr_apply (n : ℕ) (v : A.SourceLabel n)\n    (p : A.Coord n ⊕ A.Coord n) :\n    (A.stageCoordBasis n).repr v p =\n      (v : PauliCoordinateLabels I) ((A.blockIndexEquiv n p : ↥(A.coordSupport n)) : I ⊕ I) := by\n  have key : ∀ q : A.Coord n ⊕ A.Coord n,\n      ((Finsupp.lapply p).comp (A.stageCoordBasis n).repr.toLinearMap) (A.stageCoordBasis n q) =\n      ((Finsupp.lapply ((A.blockIndexEquiv n p : ↥(A.coordSupport n)) : I ⊕ I)).comp\n        ((A.SourceLabel n).subtype)) (A.stageCoordBasis n q) := by\n    intro q\n    show (A.stageCoordBasis n).repr (A.stageCoordBasis n q) p =\n      ((A.stageCoordBasis n q : A.SourceLabel n) : PauliCoordinateLabels I) _\n    rw [Module.Basis.repr_self, A.stageCoordBasis_coe n q, Finsupp.single_apply,\n      Finsupp.single_apply]\n    refine if_congr ?_ rfl rfl\n    constructor\n    · rintro rfl; rfl\n    · intro h\n      exact (A.blockIndexEquiv n).injective (Subtype.ext h)\n  have hext := Module.Basis.ext (A.stageCoordBasis n) key\n  exact congrFun (congrArg (fun f : A.SourceLabel n →ₗ[PauliBit] PauliBit => (f : _ → _)) hext) v\n\ntheorem zPart_apply (n : ℕ) (v : A.SourceLabel n) (i : A.Coord n) :\n    A.zPart n v i = (v : PauliCoordinateLabels I) (Sum.inl (i : I)) :=\n  A.stageCoordBasis_repr_apply n v (Sum.inl i)\n\ntheorem xPart_apply (n : ℕ) (v : A.SourceLabel n) (i : A.Coord n) :\n    A.xPart n v i = (v : PauliCoordinateLabels I) (Sum.inr (i : I)) :=\n  A.stageCoordBasis_repr_apply n v (Sum.inr i)\n\n--- live work status/handoff ---\nwork/FORMALIZATION-AUDIT-DECISION.md: 1: printf: Illegal option --\n# Formalization semantic-audit decision\n\nDate: 2026-08-07\n\nThe approved deliverable is a semantic audit/tutorial of the Lean\nformalization, rather than another proof package or a compilation report.\n\nThe audit will provide:\n\n1. a status summary separating proved mathematics, conditional interfaces,\n   supplied data, and unformalized claims;\n2. a dependency map from the manuscript's finite-coordinate argument through\n   the algebraic limit, concrete C-star model, GNS transport, bicommutant\n   transport, and product-factor boundary;\n3. a theorem ledger mapping each important natural-language proof sentence to\n   exact Lean declarations, hypotheses, intermediate lemmas, and semantic\n   verdicts; and\n4. a step-by-step Lean reading sequence with code excerpts and direct build or\n   `#check` commands.\n\nThe audit must keep compilation separate from mathematical validity and must\nidentify exact manuscript locators from `SOURCE-CONTRACT.md`. In particular,\nit must not call the regional hyperfinite-factor theorem proved merely because\nconditional Lean interfaces compile.\n\nThe first pass will inventory the current modules and completed-package\nreviews. Later passes will inspect the principal declarations and their proof\nchains in dependency order.\nwork/FORMALIZATION-SEMANTIC-AUDIT.md: 1: printf: Illegal option --\n# Formalization semantic audit\n\nStatus: first inventory in progress.\n\nThis document is the approved semantic/tutorial audit described in\n`FORMALIZATION-AUDIT-DECISION.md`. It is not itself a proof and does not\nchange the manuscript theorem status.\n\n## Audit verdict convention\n\n- **proved**: the stated Lean theorem follows from its explicit hypotheses and\n  compiles without placeholders;\n- **conditional**: the Lean implication is proved, but one or more hypotheses\n  are supplied structures or external analytic assumptions;\n- **infrastructure**: reusable Lean mathematics with no manuscript claim;\n- **unformalized**: a manuscript step for which no corresponding theorem is\n  currently present;\n- **not aligned**: the Lean conclusion is stronger, weaker, or materially\n  different from the natural-language sentence.\n\nCompilation, axiom reports, and mathematical alignment will be recorded\nseparately.\n\n## Source clauses\n\nThe manuscript-facing audit uses only the locators recorded in\n`SOURCE-CONTRACT.md`:\n\n- `main.tex:1671-1679`: local symplectic basis and finite-support condition;\n- `main.tex:1740-1752`: regional factor theorem statement;\n- `main.tex:1915-1920`: proposed adapted-basis star-isomorphism;\n- `main.tex:1927-1931`: pure/mixed product density state;\n- `main.tex:1945-1967`: GNS, tensor, and factor claims;\n- `main.tex:1970-2004`: quasi-equivalence and normal-folium claims.\n\n## Initial module inventory\n\nThe detailed theorem ledger and dependency graph are the next sections to be\nfilled after inspecting the principal declarations. The current theorem\ncontract itself still says:\n\n```lean\ndef regionalAlgebraTheoremStatus : String :=\n  \"conditional contract pending analytic model\"\n```\n\nThat status is consistent with the source contract and is not to be upgraded\nwithout discharging the missing finite-coordinate, representation, normality,\nand product-classification premises.\n\n## First-pass verdict\n\nThe current formalization is a sequence of conditional bridges, not yet a\nformal proof of the manuscript's regional factor theorem. The strongest\ncurrently checked route is:\n\n```text\nfinite adapted-coordinate data\n  -> finite StarAlgEquiv at each stage\n  -> coherent algebraic direct-limit StarAlgEquiv alpha\n  -> compatible algebraic state transport\n  -> supplied compatible operator representation\n  -> closed operator-range C*-algebra\n  -> supplied state-preserving C*-extension\n  -> GNS unitary and algebraic bicommutant transport\n  -> conditional product-factor/type classification\n```\n\nThe arrows are not all existence theorems. In particular, the source-specific\nfinite coordinate realization, a faithful representation of the algebraic\nlimit, the regional C*-extension, the analytic normality/WOT statements, and\nthe product-factor classification remain explicit premises or missing\nmathematics.\n\n## Status table for the reviewed overnight packages\n\n| Package | Principal Lean object | Semantic verdict | Main external premise |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| P37 | `algebraicLimitOperatorRep` | conditional theorem proved | compatible finite-stage operator representations |\n| P38 | `quasilocalCStarAlgebra` | conditional theorem proved | supplied compatible representation; stage injectivity for faithfulness |\n| P39 | `StatePreservingData`, `gnsUnitary` | conditional theorem proved | C*-completion, alpha extension, state identity and continuity |\n| P40 | `bicommutantStarEquiv`, folium transport | algebraic part proved; analytic part conditional | WOT/double-commutant and normal-functional characterizations |\n| P41 | `ProductGNSFactorization` | partial boundary only | supplied factorization/classification; infinite weight interface is incomplete |\n| P42--P46 | no reviewed candidate currently present | not yet audited | candidate/archive status must be established before use |\n\nAll five reviewed packages compile in the local project. Their closeout\nreviews explicitly separate compilation from mathematical scope. P41 is\naccepted only as partial: its infinite-pure `TracialWeightCore` does not yet\nassert positivity, normality, faithfulness, or semifiniteness.\n\n## Dependency spine and one-to-one theorem anchors\n\n### 1. Finite coordinate map\n\nNatural-language sentence:\n\n> Given finite adapted source and target word bases, send each source word to a\n> phase-corrected target word.\n\nLean anchor:\n\n```lean\nFiniteAdaptedCoordinateStarData.starEquiv\nFiniteAdaptedCoordinateStarData.starEquiv_word\nFiniteAdaptedCoordinateStarData.starEquiv_correctedWord\n```\n\nSemantic status: the construction is proved from the fields of\n`FiniteAdaptedCoordinateStarData`, but the actual manuscript-specific finite\ndata are not constructed from `main.tex:1671-1679` or `main.tex:1915-1920`.\n\n### 2. Coherence of finite maps\n\nNatural-language sentence:\n\n> The finite coordinate maps commute with the inclusions of stages.\n\nLean anchor:\n\n```lean\nstarEquiv_connecting_of_pauliBasis\nDirectedFiniteCoordinateFamily.stageEquiv_connecting\n```\n\nSemantic status: proved when word, label, phase, and connecting-map\ncompatibility are supplied.\n\n### 3. Algebraic infinite map\n\nNatural-language sentence:\n\n> Compatible finite maps descend to a unique star-isomorphism of algebraic\n> direct limits.\n\nLean anchor:\n\n```lean\nDirectedFiniteCoordinateFamily.alpha\nDirectedFiniteCoordinateFamily.alpha_of\nDirectedFiniteCoordinateFamily.existsUnique_alpha\n```\n\nSemantic status: this is a genuine algebraic direct-limit theorem, conditional\non the finite coherent family. It is not yet a C*-completion theorem.\n\n### 4. State transport\n\nNatural-language sentence:\n\n> Pull the target product state back along the algebraic alpha.\n\nLean anchor:\n\n```lean\nTargetStageStates.targetLimitState\nTargetStageStates.pulledBackState\nTargetStageStates.pulledBackState_eq_targetLimitState_alpha\nTargetStageStates.pulledBackState_isAlgebraicState\n```\n\nSemantic status: the state-level implication is proved from compatible target\nstage states. The infinite product density operator itself is not constructed\nas a von Neumann-algebraic state in this module.\n\n### 5. Algebraic operator representation\n\nNatural-language sentence:\n\n> Compatible finite-stage operator representations define a representation of\n> the quasi-local algebra.\n\nLean anchor:\n\n```lean\nalgebraicLimitOperatorRep\nalgebraicLimitOperatorRep_of\nalgebraicLimitOperatorRep_stage_congr\nalgebraicLimitOperatorRep_injective\n```\n\nSemantic status: proved conditionally. Injectivity requires stagewise\ninjectivity; no infinite tensor-product Hilbert space is constructed.\n\n### 6. Concrete C*-model\n\nNatural-language sentence:\n\n> Complete the quasi-local algebra in the operator norm.\n\nLean anchor:\n\n```lean\nOperatorRepresentation.rangeClosure\nOperatorRepresentation.embedding\nOperatorRepresentation.denseRange_embedding\n```\n\nand, for the direct-limit range,\n\n```lean\nquasilocalCStarAlgebra\nquasilocalEmbedding\ndenseRange_quasilocalEmbedding\n```\n\nSemantic status: the closure is genuinely constructed inside bounded\noperators, but only after an isometric operator representation is supplied.\nThis does not prove that the manuscript's algebra has such a representation.\n\n### 7. State-preserving GNS transport\n\nNatural-language sentence:\n\n> A state-preserving C*-isomorphism induces a canonical GNS unitary.\n\nLean anchor:\n\n```lean\nStatePreservingData.sourceState_eq_pullback\nStatePreservingData.gnsUnitary\nStatePreservingData.gnsUnitary_intertwines\nStatePreservingData.gnsConjStarAlgEquiv\n```\n\nSemantic status: proved from supplied C*-completions, state positivity/order\ndata, continuity, and an exact state identity. It is not a proof of the\nmanuscript's state identity.\n\n### 8. Bicommutant transport\n\nNatural-language sentence:\n\n> The GNS unitary identifies the represented von Neumann algebras.\n\nLean anchors:\n\n```lean\nStarSubalgebra.vonNeumannGenerated\nStarSubalgebra.le_vonNeumannGenerated\nStarSubalgebra.vonNeumannGenerated_le\nwork/TWO-LANE-FORMALIZATION-DECISION.md: 1: printf: Illegal option --\n# Two-lane formalization decision\n\nDate: 2026-08-07\n\nThe active Codex/Aristotle loop follows the two-lane plan in `PLAN.md`.\n\n**Lane G** formalizes the manuscript's general-lattice corner argument:\nthe strong-limit code projection `q`, the faithful normal finite tracial state\non `q M_Gamma q`, finiteness and fullness of `q`, and the conclusion that each\nnonzero central summand has a nonzero finite projection and hence is not type\nIII. This route does not use a direct integral and does not require a global\ntrace/weight on `M_Gamma`.\n\n**Lane H** formalizes the explicit short-range/local-hyperbolic model:\ncoherent coordinate maps, an algebraic and C-star `alpha`, the product-state\nidentity, product GNS tensor factorization, and the resulting factor and\ntrace/weight classification.\n\nThe lanes meet only after their own gates are met. In particular, the explicit\ntensor-factor result proves trivial center in the special local-hyperbolic\ncase, whereas the general corner result rules out type-III central summands\nwithout asserting trivial center.\n\nThe first approved parallel Aristotle wave is P47, P48, P52, and P54. No\ndependent packet should be submitted before its prerequisite results are\nintegrated and semantically audited.\n\nAmendment, 2026-08-07: the analytic passage from the compressed quasi-local\nC-star algebra to the von Neumann corner is mandatory project infrastructure.\nAfter P48, the loop must prove strong closedness of concrete von Neumann\nalgebras (P49A), the analytic double-commutant theorem (P49B), and Kaplansky\nunit-ball density with its compressed-corner corollary (P49C). P50 depends on\nboth the finite-stage/C-star trace P49 and the proved P49C result. These core\nanalytic theorems may require new local topology machinery, but may not be\nreplaced by axioms or supplied interfaces.\n\nAmendment, 2026-08-08: P50's checked WOT continuity is retained as a stronger\nconcrete certificate, but the field name alone is not accepted as a\nformalization of the standard ultraweak definition of normality. Package P50U\nmust define the ultraweak topology from absolutely summable series of matrix\ncoefficients, prove the topology comparison, and export an explicitly\nultraweak-normal P50 conclusion. This does not block P51's finite-projection\nargument, which uses the corner state's traciality and faithfulness rather than\nnormality.\n\nAmendment, 2026-08-08: the original P55 is retired after Aristotle returned\n`OUT_OF_BUDGET` without creating `RegionalConcreteCStarAlpha.lean`. The failed\nrun is not evidence and no code from it is integrated. Lane H now uses four\nseparate gates: P55A constructs finite-stage Pauli-to-dyadic equivalences,\nP55B proves coherence and the finite/infinite direct-limit identifications,\nP55C constructs faithful source/regional operator representations and their\nclosed ranges, and P55D extends the algebraic alpha by density. This split is\nmathematical: P53 and P54 did not yet contain an identification between their\ntwo different algebraic direct limits. P56 depends on accepted P55D.\n\nP60 may run independently of Lane H after P51 and P50U. It is optional Lane-G\nstrengthening and must use P50U's literal ultraweak-normal corner state. It may\nassume an explicitly named countable comparison family for the full corner,\nbut it may not infer a global weight from fullness alone or conceal the weight,\nnormality, faithfulness, traciality, or semifiniteness laws in an axiom.\n\nAmendment, 2026-08-08: P60 compiled and its conditional weight-series,\ntraciality, faithfulness, corner restriction, and finite-compression results\nare preserved, but P60 is not accepted as the optional global-weight theorem.\nThe closeout's P51 provenance objection was stale: P51 is accepted in\n`reviews/P51-full-finite-corner-central-exclusion-recovery.md`. The genuine\nremaining gap is standard semifiniteness on the positive cone. P60R may revise\nthe P60 candidate in place, but must prove that for each nonzero positive\n`x ∈ M` there is a nonzero positive `y ≤ x` of finite weight. It must construct\nthe required positive square-root/factorization argument from Mathlib or\nlocal proved C-star theory; that factorization may not be a new hypothesis.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
